      "language": "en",
      "text": "Hello, my name is William Coat and I'm going to show you how to tie the scrunchie or wedding crevette. First off, do up your top button on your wing collar shirt, it could be a standard wing or a deep wing depending on how you want to wear it. It goes round the collar and roughly where one of the blades comes up, in fact it's out, that should be level with one of your top button and then it's very straightforward. You take one end over the other, round the back, round the front, come up from the back, pull the way through, try not to pull the knot too tight because you want a nice big ruffled knot. You take the shorter blade, push it through the front, pull down, and then just pull up to cover your top up. You might need to look in the mirror at this point or get someone to help you and don't worry about the blade lengths because they will all be tucked under the waistcoat that will come up at least to here. All we're interested in doing is making sure we've got a nice, rich, large knot that covers your top button and makes the whole scrunch look attractive. There we go.",
